Here is the exact PowerShell script to automate your app installations using Chocolatey, followed by the DISM and OSCDIMG command workflow to create your WinPE capture media and compile your final bootable ISO.

Part 1: The Software Mass-Installation Script (Run in Audit Mode)

Run this script inside your Virtual Machine after pressing Ctrl + Shift + F3. It automatically installs Chocolatey, forces a system-wide installation context, installs your selected apps silently, and cleans up the environment.
powershell
# 1. Bypass Execution Policy for the current session
Set-ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Scope Process -Force

# 2. Install Chocolatey (System-Wide Package Manager)
[System.Net.ServicePointManager]::SecurityProtocol = [System.Net.ServicePointManager]::SecurityProtocol -bor 3072
Invoke-Expression ((New-Object System.Net.WebClient).DownloadString('https://chocolatey.org'))

# 3. Refresh environment variables so 'choco' is recognized immediately
Import-Module "$env:ProgramData\chocolatey\helpers\chocolateyProfile.psm1"
Update-SessionEnvironment

# 4. Define your software list (Change these names to match your needs)
# Note: These install machine-wide to Program Files, making them Sysprep-safe.
$Apps = @(
    "googlechrome",
    "vlc",
    "7zip",
    "notepadplusplus",
    "git"
)

# 5. Mass install the applications silently
Write-Host "Starting mass application installation..." -ForegroundColor Cyan
foreach ($App in $Apps) {
    choco install $App -y --no-progress
}

# 6. Optional: Clean up Chocolatey telemetry/caches to keep the WIM small
choco optimize
Write-Host "Installation complete! You are now ready to run Sysprep." -ForegroundColor Green
Use code with caution.

Part 2: Building WinPE & Capturing Your Custom ISO

You must run these steps on your Technician Machine (your main PC, not the VM) using the Deployment and Imaging Tools Environment command prompt (run as Administrator), which is installed via the Windows ADK.

Step 1: Create a Bootable WinPE Media (To Capture the VM)

Run these commands to build the file structure and create a bootable WinPE ISO. You will attach this ISO to your VM to boot into a command-line environment and capture its drive.
cmd
:: 1. Create the WinPE workspace files in a temporary folder
copype amd64 C:\WinPE_amd64

:: 2. Create a bootable WinPE ISO file
MakeWinMedia /ISO C:\WinPE_amd64 C:\WinPE_capture.iso
Use code with caution.

Step 2: Capture the VM's Drive to a WIM File

Boot your VM from the WinPE_capture.iso after running Sysprep. Once the WinPE command prompt opens, use DISM to capture your generalized Windows installation.
cmd
:: Capture the OS drive (usually C: or D: in WinPE) into an install.wim file
dism /Capture-Image /ImageFile:E:\install.wim /CaptureDir:C:\ /Name:"Windows11_Golden_Image" /Description:"Custom Master Image 2026" /Compress:max
Use code with caution.
(Note: Ensure E:\ points to a secondary virtual disk, a network share, or a flash drive with enough space to store the captured WIM file).

Step 3: Compile Your Final Custom OS ISO

Once you have your install.wim, copy an original Windows installation ISO's extracted files to your technician machine (e.g., C:\OS_Files). Replace C:\OS_Files\sources\install.wim with your newly captured file, and run oscdimg to build your final deployment ISO:
cmd
:: Create the final bootable installation ISO containing your custom software
oscdimg -m -o -u2 -udfver102 -bootdata:2#p0,e,bC:\OS_Files\boot\etfsboot.com#pEF,e,bC:\OS_Files\efi\microsoft\boot\efisys.bin C:\OS_Files C:\Custom_Windows_Setup.iso
Use code with caution.
